rstine Kobberøe","orcid":"0000-0003-3624-7999","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"voldstedlundpau","last":"Voldstedlund","name":"Voldstedlund, Marianne","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 10","first":"Kåre","key":"mølbakpau","last":"Mølbak","locid":"d94c7db7-f909-4a03-bdb7-185bb3eb5a96","name":"Mølbak, Kåre","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39758201"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fpubh.2024.1502893","issn":["22962565"],"journal":"Frontiers in Public Health","pages":"1502893","paperid":"1502893","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Public Health","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214091864"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-abde9d0c-16da-43fa-813f-1038901fef5b","au-f4f13187-c8fa-4857-8ae1-2cb47eadf819","ku-4ff2e1f0-a745-4b81-b57a-4b3d393c5c14","sdu-45d95c75-025b-4ea4-8944-08ab1986e294"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The increasing incidence and mortality of bacteremia in Denmark from 2010 to 2022 : a population-based nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-803794","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Except for a few countries, comprehensive all-cause surveillance for bacteremia is not part of mandatory routine public health surveillance. We argue that time has come to include automated surveillance for bacteremia in the national surveillance systems, and explore diverse approaches and challenges in establishing bacteremia monitoring. Assessed against proposed criteria, surveillance for bacteremia should be given high priority. This is based on severity, burden of illness, health gains obtained by improved treatment and prevention, risk of outbreaks (including health care associated infections), the emergence of antimicrobial drug resistance as well as the changing epidemiology of bacteremia which is seen along with an aging population and advances in medical care. The establishment of comprehensive surveillance for bacteremia was until recently conceived as an insurmountable task. With computerized systems in clinical microbiology, surveillance by real-time data capture has become achievable. This calls for re-addressing the question of including bacteremia among the conditions under mandatory surveillance. Experiences from several countries, including Denmark, show that this is feasible. We propose enhanced international collaboration, legislative action, and funding to address the challenges and opportunities.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Mølbak, Kåre","Andersen, Christian Østergaard","Dessau, Ram B.","Ellermann-Eriksen, Svend","Gubbels, Sophie","Jensen, Thøger Gorm","Knudsen, Jenny Dahl","Kristensen, Brian","Lützen, Lisbeth","Coia, John","Olesen, Bente Ruth Scharvik","Pinholt, Mette","Scheutz, Flemming","Sönksen, Ute Wolff","Søgaard, Kirstine K.","Voldstedlund, Marianne"],"cuid":["S04-100.00-803856"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Mølbak, Kåre"],"keyword":["AMR antimicrobial resistance","Artificial intelligence","Bacteremia","Bacteremia epidemiology","Blood stream infection","Denmark epidemiology","Humans","Population Surveillance methods","Public Health Surveillance","Public health","Surveillance"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mandatory surveillance of bacteremia conducted by automated monitoring","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpubh.2024.1502739","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Betalt open access"],"id":"S04-100.00-803856","identifier":[{"id":"39737463","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11683071","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85214126480","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e015a841-4b0d-450b-8e27-c7a71768a8b1","au-ef7b0b8f-e01d-4fa1-9390-eb3a2f74e059","ku-d6d01b99-640c-45e0-b37a-85b69b618e70","sdu-c0899a28-0080-457b-9e95-0b1dbd4d06f8"],"keyword":["AMR (antimicrobial resistance)","Bacteremia/epidemiology","Denmark/epidemiology","Humans","Population Surveillance/methods","Public Health Surveillance","artificial intelligence","bacteremia","blood stream infection","public health","surveillance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-16360331B48CC4D3F0772E7809331AB2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/762702959/M_lbak_et_al._2024_._Mandatory_surveillance_of_bacteremia_conducted_by_automated_