ding":null,"first":"Jacob Eifer","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"5e4d3cb6-b0a0-4541-aea1-30e73f7c10b8","name":"Møller, Jacob Eifer","orcid":"0000-0003-2873-5845","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37898098"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.amjcard.2023.09.068","issn":["00029149","18791913"],"issn_org":["00029149"],"journal":"American Journal of Cardiology","pages":"165-172","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Cardiology","title_org":"The American Journal of Cardiology","volume":"209"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174976197"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1152e356-eb05-4907-950c-709387e43182"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Psychometric Properties of the Kansas City Cardiomyopathy Questionnaire in a Surgical Population of Patients With Aortic Valve Stenosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-722907","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Author summary Polypharmacy continues to grow in importance because of multimorbid, aging populations. In healthcare, polypharmacy is well-known for its detrimental consequences related to adverse events. Polypharmacy is also a key challenge included in the precision medicine agenda. So-called precision dosing is important for addressing concomitant diseases and medications, and their impact on treatment responses. In this work, we present a study aiming at investigating this problem using real-world data from ~185 million treatment episodes leading to significant statistical power across drug-cocktails. We introduce a comprehensive analysis of dosage changes aiming to identify those significant pairs that may influence each other. More than half of the identified drug pairs were associated with readmission, mortality or longer stays and we also observed major differences in relation to disease and laboratory tests. Under the premise that drug-drug interactions are manageable through patient monitoring and dosage adjustments, we collected and cross-referenced information from a wide range of clinical and bioinformatics drug-drug interaction databases that could be related to pairs associated with dosage changes. Overall, this work shows how distinct, changing dosage patterns can facilitate the identification of drug-drug interactions in the context of polypharmacy complementing longitudinal analyses of disease progression.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Leal Rodríguez, Cristina","Haue, Amalie Dahl","Mazzoni, Gianluca","Eriksson, Robert","Biel, Jorge Hernansanz","Cantwell, Lisa","Westergaard, David","Belling, Kirstine","Brunak, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719218"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"drug dosage modifications in 000000000024 million in patient prescriptions covering eight years a danish population wide study of polypharmacy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pdig.0000336","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-719218","identifier":[{"id":"37676853","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85201626117","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10484442","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-09a88e5e-804f-46f8-9ddf-daaf66661b97"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A9C11AA0D41EA39537DAE5F4AEB3CC8C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379798090/journal.pdig.0000336.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pdig.0000336","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Brunak Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Cristina","key":"lealrodríguezpau","last":"Leal Rodríguez","locid":"37a7a684-5375-4b41-a7aa-29d286396dea","name":"Leal Rodríguez, Cristina","orcid":"0000-0002-3133-0630","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Amalie Dahl","key":"hauepau","last":"Haue","locid":"705426f3-82d0-4752-afdd-d0e50f63bf21","name":"Haue, Amalie Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-7656-7976","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gianluca","key":"mazzonipau","last":"Mazzoni","locid":"fe9d63ac-9999-4326-953b-1f7699c74210","name":"Mazzoni, Gianluca","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Robert","key":"erikssonpau","last":"Eriksson","locid":"1df7685f-b9f1-4380-a84a-81a090dbd036","name":"Eriksson, Robert","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jorge","key":"hernansanzbielpau","last":"Hernansanz Biel","locid":"d601ae00-e0cd-4325-8be6-0d80192e67ae","name":"Biel, Jorge Hernansanz","name_org":"Hernansanz Biel, Jorge","orcid":"0000-0002-3125-2951","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lisa","key":"cantwellpau","last":"Cantwell","locid":"654d5ab7-b1b9-4e80-8046-fd4eee1840a6","name":"Cantwell, Lisa","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"David","key":"westergaardpau","last":"Westergaard","locid":"049e0f46-367a-4436-9553-149dfa1b62ac","name":"Westergaard, David","orcid":"0000-0003-0128-8432","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirstine G.","key":"bellingpau","last":"Belling","locid":"47d17f91-9bfa-42d3-8dcf-fba9dff880c5","name":"Belling, Kirstine","name_org":"Belling, Kirstine G.","orcid":"0000-0001-5664-1948","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren","key":"brunakpau","last":"Brunak","locid":"9398f2a1-bef5-4491-9b57-083e6758eac2","name":"Brunak, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-0316-5866","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37676853"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pdig.0000336","issn":["27673170"],"issue":"9","journal":"PLOS Digital Health","paperid":"e0000336","status":"p","title":"PLOS Digital Health","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201626117"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-09a88e5e-804f-46f8-9ddf-daaf66661b97"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Drug dosage modifications in 24 million in-patient prescriptions covering eight years : A Danish population-wide study of polypharmacy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719218","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Pastoral livelihoods are presented with new challenges as access to land is altered by climate change and privatization. Pastoralist livelihoods however continue to be reliant on mobility and pastoralists, therefore, continue to negotiate access to land in the privatized and subdivided rangelands. Various dynamics enable and constrain pastoralists’ access under this new form of land tenure, but little work has investigated the underlying power structures of access and the importance of private property for this. Based on field work in the subdivided rangelands of Kajiado county in Kenya, we argue that social structures and formal land ownership both enable and hinder pastoralists’ access to land. Moreover, while social capital is one of the most important factors for accessing pastures in subdivided rangelands, private property rights have an overarching importance for relations of access. As a result, the group ranches’ uneven allocation of land to its members has deepened inequalities in the community.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Maja Kirstine Dahl","Hassan, Rahma"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-027257"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Kenya"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Nairobi"],"keyword":["Access","Land","Pastoralists","Private property","Social capital","Subdivision"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"private property and social capital dynamics of exclusion and sharing in the subdivided pastoral rangelands of kajiado kenya","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/367047820/Private_property_and_social_capital_-_Dynamics_of_exclusion_and_sharing_in_the_subdivided_pastoral_rangelands_of_Kajiado_Kenya_accepted_manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-027257","identifier":[{"id":"85123504074","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000745865100001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-c91a25cb-c750-476c-9174-82803dcc7f82","ku-31fe95c5-ceae-4c54-980e-48fd74fe0e43"],"keyword":["Access","land","pastoralists","private property","social capital","subdivision"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-BED9245842549A465568F7BCD4BB199C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/367047820/Private_property_and_social_capital_-_Dynamics_of_exclusion_and_sharing_in_the_subdivided_pastoral_rangelands_of_Kajiado_Kenya_accepted_manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Department of Anthropology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Global Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ke","key":"university of nairobi","loc":["Kenya","Africa"],"name":"University of Nairobi","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja Kirstine Dahl",