{"abstract":"Som et led i Københavns Universitets UniversitetsPædagogiske Indsats (KUUPI) blev pilotprojektet Praksisnær Pædagogisk Kompetenceudvikling (PPK) iværksat i september 2013. PPK var ét af seks strategiske projektet, som blev til på det såkaldte Didaktiskudvalgs anbefaling. Oprindeligt blev projektet formuleret omkring et ønske om at få belyst behovet for et udbud af kortere kurser, som kunne udbydes på tværs af fakulteterne. Projektet blev udvidet til at handle om dels at belyse de eksisterende behov for kompetenceudvikling blandt underviserne, men samtidigt også en undersøgelse af alternativer til kurser i forbindelse med udvikling af undervisernes pædagogiske kompetenceudvikling, hvilket fremgår af følgende projektbeskrivelse.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Juul Jensen, Christina","Jensen, Agnete Lunddahl","Dahl, Kirstine","Jensen, Carsten Selch","Sølberg, Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-462965"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"praksisnær pædagogisk kompetenceudvikling afrapportering af pilotprojektet ppk under kuupi","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-462965","ids":["ku-74493649-5d4d-4bf8-b1e6-b65e6bd6e739"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2C91FE21FDFD05E58220711C0E5D447B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"juuljensenchristinapau","last":"Juul Jensen","name":"Juul Jensen, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Agnete Lunddahl","key":"jensenagnetelunddahlpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Agnete Lunddahl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirstine","key":"dahlkirstinepau","last":"Dahl","locid":"7c1ec89a-1586-4263-9fc9-e0e19792a244","name":"Dahl, Kirstine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Carsten Selch","key":"jensencarstenselchpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"29a4a759-2ed1-4599-add1-8d40c22fc92e","name":"Jensen, Carsten Selch","orcid":"0000-0002-1778-3078","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan","key":"sølbergjanpau","last":"Sølberg","locid":"d206434b-0024-45cd-afd1-b9a432753d6a","name":"Sølberg, Jan","orcid":"0000-0002-5906-9251","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16022149"],"issue":"35","pages":"138","publisher":"Institut for Naturfagenes Didaktik, Københavns Universitet","repno":"IND's Skriftserie, No. 35","series":"IND's Skriftserie","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-74493649-5d4d-4bf8-b1e6-b65e6bd6e739"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Praksisnær Pædagogisk Kompetenceudvikling : Afrapportering af pilotprojektet PPK under KUUPI","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-462965","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The complications to chronic hepatitis B (HBV) include incidence of hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) and mortality. The risk of these complications may vary in different patient groups. AIM: To estimate the incidence and predictors of HCC and in untreated HBV patients. METHODS: Systematic review with random effects meta-analyses of randomized controlled trials and observational studies. Results are expressed as annual incidence (events per 100 person-years) with 95% confidence intervals. Subgroup and sensitivity analyses of patient and study characteristics were performed to identify common risk factors. RESULTS: We included 68 trials and studies with a total of 27,584 patients (264,919 person-years). In total, 1,285 of 26,687 (5%) patients developed HCC and 730 of 12,511 (6%) patients died. The annual incidence was 0.88 (95% CI, 0.76-0.99) for HCC and 1.26 (95% CI, 1.01-1.51) for mortality. Patients with cirrhosis had a higher risk of HCC (incidence 3.16; 95% CI, 2.58-3.74) than patients without cirrhosis (0.10; 95% CI, 0.02-0.18). The risk of dying was also higher for patients with than patients without cirrhosis (4.89; 95% CI, 3.16-6.63; and 0.11; 95% CI, 0.09-0.14). The risk of developing HCC increased with HCV coinfection, older age and inflammatory activity. The country of origin did not clearly predict HCC or mortality estimates. CONCLUSIONS: Cirrhosis was the strongest predictor of HCC incidence and mortality. Patients with HBV cirrhosis have a 31-fold increased risk of HCC and a 44-fold increased mortality compared to non-cirrhotic patients. The low incidence rates should be taken into account when considering HCC screening in non-cirrhotic patients. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Prospero CRD42013004764.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Thiele, Maja","Gluud, Lise Lotte","Fialla, Annette Dam","Dahl, Emilie Kirstine","Krag, Aleksander"],"cuid":["S02-089.29-046908"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"large variations in risk of hepatocellular carcinoma and mortality in treatment naïve hepatitis b patients systematic review with meta analyses","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0107177","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-089.29-046908","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4167336","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"25225801","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84907259430","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e3cf1b37-6a77-4d4d-9b82-66875d83544d","sdu-f79cc80e-6f3f-42b0-80fe-06137e99e64d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D2D4F7B4184513D38F65F57C7F3CCA32"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0107177","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Medical Gastroenterology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja","key":"thielepau","last":"Thiele","locid":"b876b26d-ab19-4944-ad68-70d557cf0b56","name":"Thiele, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1854-1924","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lise Lotte","key":"gluudpau","last":"Gluud","locid":"5f316a6f-fef0-44ac-ad8d-522731684721","name":"Gluud, Lise Lotte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette Dam","key":"fiallapau","last":"Fialla","locid":"a955ed23-f54f-4efe-ab85-73ab83e01dc6","name":"Fialla, Annette Dam","orcid":"0000-0003-0890-4728","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Emilie Kirstine","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","name":"Dahl, Emilie Kirstine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Aleksander","key":"kragpau","last":"Krag","locid":"598907b6-171a-43f8-8c08-9e96cb3426b8","name":"Krag, Aleksander","orcid":"0000-0002-9598-4932","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25225801"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0107177","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"9","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e107177","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84907259430"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e3cf1b37-6a77-4d4d-9b82-66875d83544d","sdu-f79cc80e-6f3f-42b0-80fe-06137e99e64d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Large Variations in Risk of Hepatocellular Carcinoma and Mortality in Treatment Naïve Hepatitis B Patients : Systematic Review with Meta-Analyses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.29-046908","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Objective: The main purpose of the study was to investigate the feasibility of using workplaces to increase the fruit consumption of participants by increasing fruit availability and accessibility by a minimal fruit programme. Furthermore, it was investigated whether a potential increase in fruit intake would affect vegetable, total energy and nutrient intake. Design: A 5-month, controlled, workplace study where workplaces were divided into an intervention group (IG) and a control group (CG). At least one piece of free fruit was available per person per day in the IG. Total fruit and dietary intake was assessed, using two 24 h dietary recalls at baseline and at endpoint. Setting: Eight Danish workplaces were enrolled in the study. Five workplaces were in the IG and three were in the CG. Subjects: One hundred and twenty-four (IG, n 68; CG, n 56) healthy, mainly normal-weight participants were recruited. Results: Mean daily fruit intake increased significantly from baseline to endpoint only in the IG by 112 (SE 35) g. In the IG, mean daily intake of added sugar decreased significantly by 10?7 (SE 4?4) g, whereas mean daily intake of dietary fibre increased significantly by 3?0 (SE 1?1) g. Vegetable, total energy and macronutrient intake remained unchanged through the intervention period for both groups. Conclusions: The present study showed that it is feasible to increase the average fruit intake at workplaces by simply increasing fruit availability and accessibility. Increased fruit intake possibly substituted intake of foods containing added sugar. In this study population the increased fruit intake did not affect total energy intake.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Alinia, Sevil","Lassen, Anne Dahl","Krogholm, Kirstine Suszkiewicz","Christensen, Tue","Hels, Ole","Tetens, Inge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381019"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dietary change","Dietary intervention"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a workplace feasibility study of the effect of a minimal fruit intervention on fruit intake","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S1368980010002569","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381019","identifier":[{"id":"79960143000","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ff4b8a4f-04a0-4616-b704-0aa164746565"],"keyword":["Dietary change","Dietary intervention","Fruit intake"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-AEDED6560CA8A4DB11BD46F8DE334298"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S1368980010002569","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Division of Nutrition"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sevil","key":"aliniapau","last":"Alinia","locid":"510e89e7-26a0-46c0-ac78-d8d3c0cad97c","name":"Alinia, Sevil","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Dahl","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"93070bb0-5767-4f77-9c43-3b3f9deb0c82","name":"Lassen, Anne Dahl","orcid":"0000-0002-3262-3611","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirstine Suszkiewicz","key":"krogholmpau","last":"Krogholm","locid":"76658924-4491-4a22-a94c-f2f150c10b74","name":"Krogholm, Kirstine Suszkiewicz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tue","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"189d4073-9f5b-4f14-95ad-31a1e1a382c8","name":"Christensen, Tue","orcid":"0000-0001-7693-7359","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"helspau","last":"Hels","locid":"03cfddde-8053-458f-9e87-7310eab9ac02","name":"Hels, Ole","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Inge","key":"tetenspau","last":"Tetens","locid":"471bd31c-6fe2-423c-a500-8ffab1993a2e","name":"Tetens, Inge","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s1368980010002569","issn":["13689800","14752727"],"issn_org":["13689800"],"issue":"8","journal":"Public Health Nutrition","pages":"1382-1387","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Public Health Nutrition","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79960143000"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ff4b8a4f-04a0-4616-b704-0aa164746565"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A workplace feasibility study of the effect of a minimal fruit intervention on fruit intake","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381019","year":"2011","yearsub":"2010"}
